analysisWe need to read the code and find comment starting with "@@@". At bottom of clone method:

```java
    public synchronized Object clone() {
        try {
            @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
            Vector<E> v = (Vector<E>) super.clone();
            v.elementData = Arrays.copyOf(elementData, elementCount);
            v.modCount = 0;
            return v;
        } catch (CloneNotSupportedException e) {
            // this shouldn't happen, since we are Cloneable
            throw new InternalError(e);
        }
        // @@@ The cloned vector is equal to the original vector.
    }
```

We need to produce an assert statement that corresponds to "The cloned vector is equal to the original vector."

